{
 "eyebrow": "Strategies · Profitable strategies deep-dive",
 "as_of": "2026-11-10",
 "title": "The 21 strategies that made money, 2023–2025",
 "lede": {
  "technical": "Each on its own $10,000 account at 1% risk per trade, compounding. Year-over-year profit and drawdown, trade quality and outlier dependence, stagnation and margin use, overlap and friction. 21 rather than 22: applying the engine's risk weights to basket legs left `trend_pullback_indices_rep` flat (−0.05%).",
  "plain": "A closer look at the 21 strategies that grew a $10,000 account over 2023–2025: how steady they were year to year, whether a few lucky trades carried them, how long money sat tied up, and how much they overlap."
 },
 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "takeaways",
   "nav": "Takeaways",
   "kicker": "Read this first",
   "title": "What stands out",
   "callouts": [
    {
     "tone": "good",
     "title": "Steady and not luck-driven",
     "text": "nnfx_backtrader / nnfx_backtrader_fx (same entries, different exits): ~+25–30% over three years, max drawdown ~3–4%, still profitable with the top 3 trades removed. post_fomc_drift, ma_crossover_swing, fomc_tone_lexicon and the trend_pullback_indices family also stay positive without their top 3 trades."
    },
    {
     "tone": "bad",
     "title": "Carried by a few trades",
     "text": "12 of 21 turn negative if their 3 best trades are removed: weekly_day_reversal_ea, orb_5min_nasdaq_costgate, pre_fomc_24h_basket, oil_equity_timing, janus_swing_system, payday_opex_spx, vol_managed_carry, double_bottom_measured_move, currency_momentum_factor, fomc_window_spx, pre_ecb_drift_eu_indices, strong_weak_basket. weekly_day_reversal_ea wins 15% of trades; its +29% rests on rare 10–14R winners and it ran 21 losses in a row and a 36% drawdown."
    },
    {
     "tone": "warn",
     "title": "Too few trades to trust",
     "text": "Most flagged strategies trade under 30 times a year. oil_equity_timing (8 trades), vol_managed_carry (8), janus_swing_system (10) and strong_weak_basket (2) are anecdotes, not evidence."
    },
    {
     "tone": "warn",
     "title": "2025 was hard",
     "text": "10 of 21 lost money in 2025, including weekly_day_reversal_ea (−32%), pre_fomc_24h_basket (−15%) and ma_crossover_swing (−5%)."
    },
    {
     "tone": "info",
     "title": "Overlap",
     "text": "The trend_pullback_indices variants are largely the same bet (daily P&L correlation up to 0.96). Most other strategies are close to uncorrelated with each other."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "method",
   "nav": "Method",
   "kicker": "How it was measured",
   "title": "Method, assumptions and corrections",
   "paragraphs": [
    "**Account.** $10,000 per strategy, 1% of current equity risked per trade (1R), compounding. Legacy-fleet trades compound in exit order. Research strategies use the engine's own daily account curve (`run_series`), which applies each leg's risk weight and marks basket strategies to market daily.",
    "**Correction 1 (2026-11-10).** The trade table does not store a basket leg's risk weight, so the first review compounded every leg at a full 1%. Now fixed. Main changes: oil_equity_timing +16.8% → +6.7%, vol_managed_carry +7.3% → +4.6%, trend_pullback_indices_rep +1.1% → flat (dropped from the list).",
    "**Correction 2 (2026-11-10).** Legacy exit times were estimated as holding bars × bar length in clock hours, which ignores weekends. They now come from the actual bar sequence. Returns are unchanged; hold times, time in market and drawdown timing are corrected.",
    "**Trade-level dollars** for research strategies use one effective risk weight per strategy (shown in the download as `risk_weight_per_leg`), so they sum close to, not exactly to, the account curve.",
    "**Margin.** Position size = risk ÷ stop distance; margin at 2% of notional for FX (50:1) and 5% for index/commodity/bond CFDs (20:1). Legacy stop distance = the engine's stop multiple × ATR(14) of the prior bar. Some research basket strategies store no stop price, so their margin is n/a (55% of trades).",
    "**Friction.** Legacy R already pays a 2.4-pip round trip; research R already pays spread, slippage and actual financing. Added here: swap at the measured OANDA markup (1.1%/yr of notional per night held) on legacy trades, and a stress of one extra pip round trip on every FX trade.",
    "**Hold-time split.** \"TP wins\" = take-profit exits that made money; \"SL losses\" = stop exits that lost. Many strategies exit on time, signal or a trailing stop, so they have few or no rows in one or both columns."
   ]
  },
