  {
   "id": "overlap",
   "nav": "Overlap & friction",
   "kicker": "4 · Portfolio overlap and friction",
   "title": "Do they overlap, and what do costs do?",
   "paragraphs": [
    "**All 21 on one $10,000 account** at a fixed $100 (1%) risk per trade: up to **50 trades open at once** (on 2025-08-22), and margin peaked at **$12,581 (126% of the account)** on 2024-06-12 — counting only trades with a known stop, so the true peak is higher. Running all of them together on $10,000 would breach margin; it needs either a bigger account, lower risk per trade, or fewer strategies.",
    "**Correlated pairs (|ρ| ≥ 0.5):** `trend_pullback_indices` ↔ `trend_pullback_indices_trades` 0.96; `trend_pullback_indices_sma5` ↔ `trend_pullback_indices13` 0.86; `trend_pullback_indices_sma5` ↔ `trend_pullback_indices` 0.65; `trend_pullback_indices_sma5` ↔ `trend_pullback_indices_trades` 0.63; `oil_equity_timing` ↔ `trend_pullback_indices13` 0.61; `trend_pullback_indices_sma5` ↔ `oil_equity_timing` 0.54."
